Found the issue. On line 46:

```swift
if hasCompletedOnboarding && isPremium {
    MainTabView()
} else {
    OnboardingContainerView()
}
```

When you tap Continue, `completeOnboarding()` sets `hasCompletedOnboarding = true`, but the app also requires `isPremium == true` to show `MainTabView`. Since `isPremium` is false (or becomes false after the subscription check on line 59), you stay stuck on the onboarding screen.

The screen time permission is the **last** onboarding step (`.screenTimePermission`), so after tapping Continue it sets `hasCompletedOnboarding = true` but you're still shown `OnboardingContainerView()` because `isPremium` is false — and the container just shows the same last screen again.

The fix: the pricing/payment step (`.pricing`) needs to come **before** or the navigation condition needs to handle the case where onboarding is complete but premium isn't purchased yet. 

